---
interface Props {
  heading?: string | null;
}
const { heading = 'Insert vs. full-frame: what actually stays?' } = Astro.props;
---
<figure class="replacement-diagram">
  {heading && <figcaption class="diagram-heading">{heading}</figcaption>}
  <p class="diagram-intro">These are two different scopes of work. The cleanest way to tell them apart is to follow the <strong>existing frame</strong>.</p>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card method-insert">
      <header class="method-head">
        <span class="method-number">01</span>
        <div><p>INSERT / POCKET</p><h3>The existing frame stays</h3></div>
      </header>
      <div class="method-visual">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 860 430" role="img" aria-label="Cross section showing a wall opening with the existing window frame left in place and a new window fitted inside the old frame.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="insert-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 Z" class="insert-marker"/></marker>
          </defs>
          <rect x="20" y="20" width="820" height="390" rx="16" class="field"/>
          <rect x="70" y="92" width="720" height="74" class="siding"/>
          <rect x="70" y="166" width="720" height="40" class="wrb"/>
          <rect x="70" y="206" width="110" height="166" class="stud"/>
          <rect x="680" y="206" width="110" height="166" class="stud"/>
          <rect x="180" y="204" width="55" height="168" class="old-frame"/>
          <rect x="625" y="204" width="55" height="168" class="old-frame"/>
          <rect x="235" y="222" width="390" height="132" rx="4" class="new-window"/>
          <line x1="430" y1="222" x2="430" y2="354" class="mullion"/>
          <rect x="235" y="350" width="390" height="16" class="interior-stop"/>

          <line x1="208" y1="185" x2="208" y2="78" class="leader insert" marker-end="url(#insert-arrow)"/>
          <text x="208" y="58" class="callout insert-text">EXISTING FRAME</text>
          <text x="208" y="76" class="supporting">remains in the opening</text>

          <line x1="430" y1="240" x2="430" y2="390" class="leader"/>
          <text x="430" y="402" class="callout center">NEW WINDOW FITS INSIDE IT</text>

          <text x="125" y="255" class="structure">WALL</text>
          <text x="735" y="255" class="structure">WALL</text>
          <text x="208" y="300" class="frame-label">OLD FRAME</text>
          <text x="430" y="298" class="window-label">NEW WINDOW</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="method-summary"><strong>What changes:</strong> the window unit. Most of the surrounding finish and the existing frame remain.</div>
      <div class="method-fit"><strong>Usually considered when</strong><span>the existing frame is sound, serviceable, and the opening does not require reconstruction.</span></div>
    </article>

    <article class="method-card method-full">
      <header class="method-head">
        <span class="method-number">02</span>
        <div><p>FULL-FRAME</p><h3>The old window frame comes out</h3></div>
      </header>
      <div class="method-visual">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 860 430" role="img" aria-label="Cross section showing the old window frame removed from the opening, the rough opening exposed, new flashing installed, and a new window installed to the opening.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="full-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 Z" class="full-marker"/></marker>
          </defs>
          <rect x="20" y="20" width="820" height="390" rx="16" class="field"/>
          <rect x="70" y="92" width="720" height="74" class="siding"/>
          <rect x="70" y="166" width="720" height="40" class="wrb"/>
          <rect x="70" y="206" width="110" height="166" class="stud"/>
          <rect x="680" y="206" width="110" height="166" class="stud"/>
          <path d="M180 206 H680 V372 H180 Z" class="rough-opening"/>
          <path d="M180 206 H680" class="head-flash"/>
          <path d="M180 206 V372" class="jamb-flash"/>
          <path d="M680 206 V372" class="jamb-flash"/>
          <path d="M180 372 H680" class="sill-flash"/>
          <rect x="205" y="222" width="450" height="132" rx="4" class="new-window"/>
          <line x1="430" y1="222" x2="430" y2="354" class="mullion"/>

          <line x1="300" y1="194" x2="300" y2="78" class="leader full" marker-end="url(#full-arrow)"/>
          <text x="300" y="58" class="callout full-text">OLD FRAME REMOVED</text>
          <text x="300" y="76" class="supporting">rough opening is exposed</text>

          <line x1="430" y1="395" x2="430" y2="366" class="leader full"/>
          <text x="430" y="403" class="callout center">NEW WINDOW STARTS AT THE OPENING</text>

          <text x="125" y="255" class="structure">WALL</text>
          <text x="735" y="255" class="structure">WALL</text>
          <text x="430" y="198" class="flash-label">RE-FLASH OPENING</text>
          <text x="430" y="298" class="window-label">NEW WINDOW</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="method-summary"><strong>What changes:</strong> the old frame and surrounding assembly are opened up so the new window can be installed from the rough opening outward.</div>
      <div class="method-fit"><strong>Usually considered when</strong><span>the existing frame is damaged, the opening needs correction, or the project calls for more complete reconstruction.</span></div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="decision-strip"><strong>Do not choose the method from the product brochure.</strong><span>Choose it from the existing opening and frame condition at the house.</span></div>
</figure>

<style>
  .replacement-diagram{margin:0}.diagram-heading{display:block;margin:0 0 var(--space-2xs);font-size:var(--step-2);font-weight:650;letter-spacing:var(--tracking-display);line-height:var(--leading-display)}.diagram-intro{margin:0 0 var(--space-l);max-width:70ch;color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:var(--step--1)}.diagram-intro strong{color:var(--ink)}
  .method-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:var(--space-l)}.method-card{padding:var(--space-m);border:1px solid var(--line);border-top:4px solid var(--ink);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);background:var(--paper-raised)}.method-insert{border-top-color:var(--accent)}.method-full{border-top-color:var(--danger)}
  .method-head{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem 1fr;gap:var(--space-s);align-items:center;margin-bottom:var(--space-s)}.method-number{display:grid;width:2.8rem;height:2.8rem;place-items:center;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);font-weight:750}.method-insert .method-number{background:var(--accent)}.method-full .method-number{background:var(--danger)}.method-head p{margin:0 0 .15rem;color:var(--ink-faint);font-size:var(--step--2);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:var(--tracking-label)}.method-head h3{margin:0;font-size:var(--step-1);line-height:1.12}
  .method-visual{overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius);background:var(--paper-sunk)}.method-visual svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.field{fill:var(--paper-sunk);stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1.5}.siding{fill:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 13%,transparent)}.wrb{fill:color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent) 9%,transparent);stroke:var(--accent-ink);stroke-width:1}.stud{fill:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 17%,transparent)}.old-frame{fill:color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent) 22%,transparent);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:3}.new-window{fill:var(--paper-raised);stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:3}.mullion{stroke:var(--ink-soft);stroke-width:2}.interior-stop{fill:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 16%,transparent)}.rough-opening{fill:color-mix(in srgb,var(--danger) 5%,transparent);stroke:var(--danger);stroke-width:3;stroke-dasharray:10 7}.head-flash,.jamb-flash,.sill-flash{stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:9;fill:none}.sill-flash{stroke-width:11}.leader{fill:none;stroke:var(--ink-soft);stroke-width:2}.leader.insert{stroke:var(--accent)}.leader.full{stroke:var(--danger)}.insert-marker{fill:var(--accent)}.full-marker{fill:var(--danger)}.callout{fill:var(--ink);font:750 12px Outfit,system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-anchor:middle}.insert-text{fill:var(--accent-ink)}.full-text{fill:var(--danger)}.supporting{fill:var(--ink-soft);font:550 11px Outfit,system-ui,sans-serif;text-anchor:middle}.center{text-anchor:middle}.structure{fill:var(--ink-faint);font:750 11px Outfit,system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.12em;text-anchor:middle}.frame-label{fill:var(--accent-ink);font:700 10px Outfit,system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-anchor:middle}.window-label{fill:var(--ink);font:750 14px Outfit,system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-anchor:middle}.flash-label{fill:var(--accent-ink);font:750 11px Outfit,system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;text-anchor:middle}
  .method-summary{margin-top:var(--space-s);padding:.8rem .9rem;border-left:3px solid var(--ink);background:var(--paper-sunk);font-size:var(--step--1);color:var(--ink-soft)}.method-insert .method-summary{border-left-color:var(--accent)}.method-full .method-summary{border-left-color:var(--danger)}.method-summary strong{color:var(--ink)}.method-fit{display:grid;gap:.18rem;margin-top:var(--space-s);padding-top:var(--space-s);border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.method-fit strong{text-transform:uppercase;font-size:var(--step--2);letter-spacing:var(--tracking-label);color:var(--ink-faint)}.method-fit span{font-size:var(--step--1);color:var(--ink-soft)}.decision-strip{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:var(--space-s);align-items:baseline;margin-top:var(--space-l);padding:var(--space-s) var(--space-m);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:3px solid var(--ink);background:var(--paper-raised);font-size:var(--step--1)}.decision-strip strong{color:var(--ink)}.decision-strip span{color:var(--ink-soft)}
  @media(max-width:900px){.method-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:620px){.decision-strip{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.25rem}}
</style>
